+### User transfer (between organizations)
+
+- Only an org admin of the organization in the path may transfer its users
+  (non-admins → 403). An organization other than the caller's → 404.
+- The user must belong to the organization in the path; otherwise → 404.
+- The target `toOrgId` must be set (400), differ from the current organization
+  (400), and exist (400). Organizations have no table; one exists when at least
+  one user belongs to it.
+- A user who is a member of any project cannot be transferred (400). Remove the
+  memberships first: project members belong to the project's organization.
+- The transferred user loses org admin rights. Admin rights are per organization.
+- Transfers are all or nothing.
+
